.TH FOUNDATION-CLI 1 "October 2026" "software-foundation 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
foundation-cli \- validate and print a bounded collection of text entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B foundation-cli
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version | \-\-self-check ]
.br
.B foundation-cli \-\-
.I TEXT
.RI [ TEXT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command validates the complete request before printing any entries.
Each entry must contain 1 through 256 printable ASCII bytes.
At most 64 entries are accepted in one request. Duplicate entries are allowed.
Successful output contains a decimal identifier, a tab, the original text and
a newline for each entry. Identifiers begin at 1 for each invocation.
.PP
Quote each entry according to the invoking shell. The application does not
interpret text as a shell command. No persistent collection is created.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command usage. Invoking the command without arguments has the same effect.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application name and version.
.TP
.B \-\-self-check
Check a small library operation without creating user files or requiring a display.
.TP
.B \-\-
End command-option processing. Every remaining argument is one text entry,
including arguments that begin with a dash. At least one entry is required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The complete operation succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Input validation, capacity, runtime or output writing failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line has an unsupported option or missing entry.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
foundation-cli \-\- "First entry" "Second entry"
foundation-cli \-\- "\-\-literal-text"
foundation-cli \-\-self-check
.fi
.SH FILES
The command has no configuration file and writes no persistent state.
Keep the complete installed package together when moving a portable archive.
.SH NOTES
The browser-target developer package runs this CLI using the retained Node
runtime. Keep the matching JavaScript and WebAssembly files together.
Native packages use the ordinary executable directly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR software-foundation (7)
